# The kernel's `mprotect` and `mmap` contracts: a successful
# `mprotect(PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE)` that covered a token's bytes left them
# this process's, readable and writable (never downgraded or unmapped
# since: tokens cover only metadata-region bytes), and they read as zero.
Unbacked::commit	platform/kernel fact	none (assumption)
# Page protection is not modeled: a lazily committed table's owner reads
# and writes only the pages it has committed.
Unbacked::into_lazy	platform/kernel fact	none (assumption)
